cff-version: 1.2.0

message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the archived software release,
  the associated research article, and the associated dataset using
  the metadata provided in this file.

title: >-
  Neighbor-Sentiment: Python-MATLAB implementation for flexible feature extraction in Spanish tweet sentiment analysis

type: software

abstract: >-
  Research software associated with the article "A novel flexible
  feature extraction algorithm for Spanish tweet sentiment analysis
  based on the context of words". The main executable,
  feature_combination_14engs.py, is written in Python and controls
  the experimental workflow. The Python program invokes algorithms
  and supporting functions implemented in 23 MATLAB source files.
  The reference environment uses Python 3.8.8, MATLAB R2020b, and
  the MATLAB Engine API for Python. The software implements the
  Neighbor-Sentiment method, which uses flexible word-level feature
  extraction, grouping genetic algorithms, individual classifiers,
  and a voting procedure for sentiment analysis of Spanish tweets.

